  "body": "Reported by the maintainer in chat on 2026-11-16, build v0.22.0 `ef1f5345`; filed by an agent:\n\n> \"the model imported (fig8.step in testdata) - has chamfer so the edge below the chamfer look like this ... an enormous amount of small sections rather than a welded edge like the one above.\"\n\n## What happens\n\n1. Import `fig8.step`. The model has a swept (figure-eight) wall with a chamfer at its top.\n2. Add a 2D Adaptive. On the Geometry tab set \"Click selects\" to Edges.\n3. Click the upper edge of the chamfer. The pick is one edge: `Chain fig8 · open · 113.1 mm · 1 of 1`.\n4. Click the edge below the chamfer (chamfer to wall). Each click picks a piece of about 0.9 mm. Four Ctrl+clicks give `Chain fig8 · open · 0.9 mm · 1 of 4` to `4 of 4`.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe edge below the chamfer is one feature edge, as the edge above it is. One click picks its full length. A chain made from it has one row.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n- The user cannot select this edge for a 2D operation in practice: an edge of about 113 mm needs more than 100 clicks.\n- A chain of many short open pieces can give a toolpath with many short moves, or a refusal, where one smooth chain is correct.\n- The rule of #692 says that only feature edges are pickable, never tessellation edges. These pieces look like tessellation or patch joints that the pick shows as feature edges.\n\n## Where to look\n\n- Find if the STEP file has this edge as many short edges (a chamfer made of many small faces), or if the kernel import or `decompose` splits one curve.\n- If the file has many short edges that are tangent-continuous: join them to one pickable feature edge at import or at the pick (G1 chain below an angle limit).\n- If the import splits one curve: keep the curve as one edge.\n- Compare with the upper chamfer edge of the same model, which is one edge.\n\nWorkaround: Shift+click picks the whole loop, where the loop is the wanted geometry.\n\nSafety floor: the change is in model geometry or its edge topology, which feeds chains and toolpaths. Thus `effort:high`.\n\nRelated: #692 (feature edges only), #1505 (edge picking), #2201 (slow frames while an edge is selected, same model and session).\n\nDone means: on `fig8.step`, one click on the edge below the chamfer picks the full edge as one chain row, and a test on that file pins the edge count of the chamfer's lower boundary.\n",
